{"author":{"id":"dec876858d28babbadcead4137861bf586626b8518cbce9c5f4fc52ac3b424b8"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790966793,"nonce":"NBZhYK9WEvEFp21bItewri4yI6U=","title":"Group header chrome chips (edit / × / chevron) align to the title line only — when the","message":"**Bug.** Group header chrome chips (edit pencil / delete × / collapse chevron) align flex-start-vertically with the title row. When the group's description wraps to 2+ visual lines, the header band stretches downward to fit the wrapped lines but the chrome chips stay pinned at the title's y-coordinate. Looks fine but the band feels lopsided — chips at top-right while the description fills the lower portion of the band on its own.\n\nReported with a screenshot: \"New Group / Group created from / multi-select\" wraps to two lines under the title; chrome row sits at the title baseline.\n\n**Why:** In `compute_group_slots` ([packages/blinc_node_editor/src/slot.rs:486](packages/blinc_node_editor/src/slot.rs#L486)) the header is a flex-row with `align_items: FlexStart`, and each chrome chip carries a manually-computed `top` margin equal to `(title_line - chrome_size) * 0.5` so the chip baselines align with the title row's centre — not with the centre of the full header (title + description rows). When the description grows multiline the header height grows but the chrome margin doesn't track.\n\n**How to apply:** When fixing, either:\n1. Switch the header to `align_items: Center` and drop the manual `top` margins on chrome chips — they then ride the vertical centre of the live header rect.\n2. Keep top-aligned but anchor the chrome row to the title-row centre explicitly (clamp the chip's `top` margin against the resolved title rect's y).\n\nOption 1 is the smaller change but visually moves the chips down when the description wraps; option 2 keeps the chips at the title row regardless of description length (closer to current behaviour but properly normalised).\n\nUser preference unrecorded — ask before changing.\n\nRelated: gotcha text min content inflation — different bug, similar shape (text wrapping inflating parent height in unintended ways).","files":null}]}